Appended to the independent review; sections 1-5 left unedited per never-prune.

Guards (commit 0c84a3a4fc) verdict: SOUND. All ten mutations go RED --
deleting either path rule, narrowing .git to is_dir(), widening results to a
substring, making either distinct count decorative, flipping fail-closed to
fail-open, flipping outside_root to live_run, silencing the exclusion report,
and dropping the --include-non-live warning. No decorative pattern. Keying
.git on exists() not is_dir() closes the worktree case before it was raised,
and is tested by name.

Fire counts: 112 kept / 1139 excluded on the default root, matching the
independent count exactly; 971 excluded at repo root, which includes the 27
live results/arc_e3 files -- defensible for a live-generator rate, and they
stay reachable via --roots results/arc_e3.

Two gaps, both verified against the shipped code:
- the sweep root ITSELF is never tested for .git, so a clone passed as the
  root sweeps clean; abpin is caught today only because it happens to hold a
  results/ dir.
- classify_path raises PermissionError on an unreadable ancestor, though
  rglob skips such dirs first, so the real effect is a silently smaller N.

The distinct-count guard is load-bearing: it is the only thing that sees the
16.4% duplication inside the live population, and it does -- 112 scored, 93
distinct files, 87 distinct predicates.

One correction needed. The new branch-count warning is right in substance and
wrong in its evidence: no model has 376 or 356 branches (actual maxima 435 and
358), and in the live population the four cited memorisers rank 21st, 9th,
64th and 8th. The top live model, sk48 at 212, is genuine perception. The
caution holds restated: 5 of the top 20 by branches have a broken goal
predicate versus 1 of the bottom 20.

